Step 4: Complete Security Hardening (Run on EC2)
Run these commands directly in your EC2 terminal session:

1. Create Non-Root deploy User & Copy SSH Keys

# Create the deploy user and add to sudo group
sudo adduser --disabled-password --gecos "" deploy
sudo usermod -aG sudo deploy

# Give deploy user passwordless sudo privileges (required for automation)
echo "deploy ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL" | sudo tee /etc/sudoers.d/deploy

# Copy your authorized_keys to deploy user
sudo mkdir -p /home/deploy/.ssh
sudo cp ~/.ssh/authorized_keys /home/deploy/.ssh/
sudo chown -R deploy:deploy /home/deploy/.ssh
sudo chmod 700 /home/deploy/.ssh
sudo chmod 600 /home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys

2. Update SSH Daemon Settings

Open the SSH configuration file:
sudo nano /etc/ssh/sshd_config

Use Ctrl + W to search and update (or add) these three directives:
Change Port 22 to Port 2222 (make sure to remove # if present)
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
Save and exit: Ctrl + O  Ctrl + X.

3. Configure UFW Firewall

sudo ufw default deny incoming
sudo ufw default allow outgoing
sudo ufw allow 2222/tcp comment 'Custom SSH Port'
sudo ufw allow 80/tcp comment 'HTTP'
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'HTTPS'
sudo ufw enable

